@ 10.2.6.2 - Proto-North Sarawak to Proto-Kenyah
# citation: Whimemsz, from Blust, Robert (2007), “Òma Lóngh Historical Phonology”. Oceanic Linguistics 46(1):1 – 53 Word-initial nasals assimilate to the POA of a following consonant
	d > l / #_ (sporadic)
	ʀ > h / V_V(C)#
	ʀ > h / _#
	ɻ > ∅
	s > h / _#
	{ i, u } > { e, o } / _h#
	h > ∅ / _#
	S > S:[-voice] / _#
	l > n / _#
	s > t / _VsVC
	CV > ∅ / _NCVC (in reduplications)